// @ens-test --jobs 1
// @exit 2
// @stdout-contains PASS first test passes
// @stdout-contains panic: boom
// @stdout-contains crash_test.ens
// @stderr-contains the test program stopped with code
// @stderr-contains while running 'second test panics'. Run that test alone with 'ens test --filter "second test panics"' to see its output
// A panic in the second test ends the whole run. With one job the tests run one after another, so
// the first result is already out, and what the suite reported on its error stream follows the
// results on that same stream. The command saw which test had started and not finished, so it
// names the test.
